course: dictionary
lesson: 5719
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Taz of Looney Tunes spins like a tornado and eats everything.» Spinning like a tornado and eating everything is wild and silly, so looney means crazy or very silly here. Check it: swap in silly and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: A looney can also be a person. Calling someone «a looney» is rude, and it can hurt their feelings, especially people who have a mental illness. Kind words matter, so choose yours with care.
explain: In Canada, «the loonie» is a coin, not a silly word at all. Look at the sentence around the word to find out which meaning is meant: a cartoon, a person, or money.
fact: Looney means crazy or very silly, and it is an informal word.
fact: A looney is a rude word for a person who acts in a crazy way, and it can hurt people.
fact: Looney is also spelled «loony», and both spellings are used.
fact: In Canada, a loonie is the one-dollar coin, and it has a loon bird on it.
fact: A toonie is the Canadian two-dollar coin. «Looney Tunes» is a famous cartoon, and it is full of wild, silly characters.
exercise: «Taz of Looney Tunes spins like a tornado and eats everything.» What does looney mean here? | A one-dollar coin | Very tired | Sad and quiet | *Wild and silly
exercise: In Canada, a «loonie» is what? | A two-dollar coin | *A one-dollar coin with a loon bird on it | A kind of cartoon dog | A rude name for a teacher
exercise: Why should you be careful about calling someone a looney? | It means they are very tall | It means they are very rich | It is always a polite word | *It can be hurtful, especially to people with mental illness
test: What is a «toonie» in Canada? | A loon bird | A cartoon character | A one-dollar coin | *A two-dollar coin
test: What does «a looney idea» mean? | A quiet, sleepy idea | *A crazy or silly idea | A kind and sensible plan | A one-dollar coin
exam: Why is calling a person «a looney» unkind? | Because it means they are a famous cartoon | *Because it is rude and can hurt their feelings | Because it is the name of a coin | Because it always means they are clever
